"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:43:32-07:00","id":936701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931647-new-supernatural-fighting-style-ideas?p=936642#post936642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Adamantine Hand a horror of game design? I don't remember it that much, but I remember it making me weep and cry.</div> </div> </div> </div>One high dot involved taking aggravated damage for some crappy effect or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:54:17-07:00","id":936730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931647-new-supernatural-fighting-style-ideas?p=936701#post936701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One high dot involved taking aggravated damage for some crappy effect or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the effects give you minor benefits against/with a single Arcana.<br /> <br /> The feature you're talking about? Take Aggravated damage, get bonus dice on a spellcasting roll!<br /> <br /> For one Arcana. On a one-for-one basis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T06:54:56-07:00","id":937056,"title":"","content":"Adamantine Hand was really fucking sad.<br /> <br /> I'll just fetch it:<br /> <br /> <b>Fighting Style: Adamantine Hand (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Five dots of Fighting Style Merits (at least one of which must have \u2022\u2022\u2022 ranks), Awakened, Arcanum \u2022 (see below), Adamantine Arrow Status \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your character has learned to manipulate magical energies with physical techniques, above and beyond rote mudras. You must purchase this Fighting Style separately for each Arcanum (so there is the Death Hand, the Hand of Space and so on). Your character must have one more dot in the associated Arcanum than the dots of the maneuver you wish him to learn. Just as other Fighting styles, you must purchase each maneuver in order. This rule applies, separately, to each style. For example, a character with Adamantine Hand: Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Adamantine Hand: Life \u2022 can progress to Adamantine Hand: Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or Adamantine Hand: Life \u2022\u2022 \u2014 not \u2022\u2022\u2022. The names below are often used in old texts, but every school has a unique, cryptic name for each technique.<br /> <br /> <b>Thunder (\u2022)</b>: Your character can sense the weak points in Shielding Practice spells without even using magic. Her psychic senses intuitively seek out flaws in these defenses, and she knows how to physically slip through them. If an opponent employs a Shielding spell using the Fighting Style\u2019s Arcanum, reduce the spell\u2019s effect by one point against the character\u2019s spells, Brawl strikes or Weaponry attacks. Drawback: The character must make physical contact with a hand or held weapon, even when casting a spell, in order to benefit from this maneuver.<br /> <br /> <b>Diamond (\u2022\u2022)</b>: Your character can alter her Shielding spells if they belong to the Fighting Style\u2019s Arcanum. She dodges away from weak points in her shield and concentrates its strength in a reduced area. She can increase the strength of her shield by one point against one oncoming attack per turn, but suffers a one-point reduction in shield strength against all other attacks in that turn. She can improve or degrade the shield against different attacks or opponents on each turn. If your character learns the third rank of the Fighting Style\u2019s Arcanum, she can change the adjustment to +2/\u20132 if she wishes. She can apply this benefit to advanced spells that protect others, but only if she\u2019s adjacent to the individual or group she\u2019s protecting. Drawback: Using this maneuver costs one point of Willpower per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Star (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b>: Your character may cast a spell from the Fighting Style\u2019s Arcanum and perform a physical action in the same turn. The spellcasting roll suffers a \u20131 die penalty. Drawback: This maneuver costs one point of Willpower per turn. Your character may not combine this maneuver with other abilities that grant multiple actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b>: Your character can sacrifice her own life force to enhance a spell from the Fighting Style\u2019s Arcanum. She can choose to suffer as many points of aggravated damage as her Resolve. Each point of damage coverts into a bonus die on her spellcasting for that turn. She can also choose to make the damage resistant to magical and Mana-based healing to give the spellcasting roll the 9-again quality. Drawback: This maneuver costs one point of Willpower per use.<br /> <br /> <b>Abyss (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b>: Your character hones the bond between her soul and body to such an extent that she can channel Supernal energies physically, without tempting of the Abyss. She does not suffer Paradoxes when she casts spells using the Fighting Style\u2019s Arcanum if she channels them through physical contact. In combat, she must successfully initiate a grapple to use this maneuver on a moving target.<br /> <br /> Truly terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:26:53-07:00","id":937163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931647-new-supernatural-fighting-style-ideas?p=937056#post937056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fighting Style: Adamantine Hand (\u2022 to <u><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></u>) </b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Five dots of Fighting Style Merits (at least one of which must have \u2022\u2022\u2022 ranks), Awakened, Arcanum \u2022 (see below), Adamantine Arrow Status \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your character has learned to manipulate magical energies with physical techniques, above and beyond rote mudras. You must purchase this Fighting Style separately for each Arcanum (so there is the Death Hand, the Hand of Space and so on). <u><b>Your character must have one more dot in the associated Arcanum than the dots of the maneuver you wish him to learn.</b></u> Just as other Fighting styles, you must purchase each maneuver in order. This rule applies, separately, to each style. For example, a character with Adamantine Hand: Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Adamantine Hand: Life \u2022 can progress to Adamantine Hand: Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or Adamantine Hand: Life \u2022\u2022 \u2014 not \u2022\u2022\u2022. The names below are often used in old texts, but every school has a unique, cryptic name for each technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you can't even complete the style unless you are an Archmaster? Epic...Fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:32:33-07:00","id":937164,"title":"","content":"Oh god, I didn't even remember that. Yeah, that's...not good. I was thinking more of the supernatural style merits from Hurt Locker or the Extra Limbs fighting style from Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:06:47-07:00","id":937177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931647-new-supernatural-fighting-style-ideas?p=937163#post937163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you can't even complete the style unless you are an Archmaster? Epic...Fail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said:<br /> <br /> <i>Really</i> sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:57:43-07:00","id":937198,"title":"","content":"I had a character that had the first three dots (explicitly for the third dot) and it's pretty fucking rad. -1 die for getting to punch people while casting spells, all while under the effects of that Forces+Life spell that turns you into a fire-dude, was a lot of fun at worst and really effective at best.<br /> <br /> And the 5th dot being unattainable by a normal Mage is fine, considering it's a <i>way to completely ignore paradox</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:50:58-07:00","id":942387,"title":"","content":"It's a shame that Adamantine Hand (and Awakening in general) doesn't really work, because a magic martial arts style is a pretty great idea. <br /> <br /> Another idea in the vein of High Speed Combat: Aerial Maneuvers. Basically, a Movement Style for characters who can fly that lets them do cool flying stuff. <br /> <br /> I had a bunch of style merits for my Mage remake designed to cover things that could come up there too. Power Armor Operation, Dogfighting, and Bridge Command were in (there's a heavy emphasis on mad science), and they're designed to not be Mage-exclusive and as broad as possible. So if you're playing a historical game set during the Golden Age of Piracy, you could use Bridge Command on a pirate ship. Or a TFV agent with experimental powered armor or even an AKD agent with a suit of enchanted armor could use Power Armor Operation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}